Thought: Having skip_connect on 1<-0 (the input edge) hurt performance (0.393667). It seems the input edge benefits from a convolution. The best config so far is 0.446500 with nor_conv_3x3 on 1<-0, 2<-1, 3<-0, 3<-1 and skip_connect on 2<-0, 3<-2.

Let me try nor_conv_1x1 in place of some skip_connects to see if that helps. Also, I should explore the effect of the 3<-2 edge since it connects node 2 to node 3.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "nor_conv_1x1", "2<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-2": "nor_conv_1x1"}
